12
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:40,530
First, what is safety?

13
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:41,730
What is safety?

14
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:43,730
You can answer it like this.

15
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:47,330
Safety is defined as the freedom from those conditions

16
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:50,930
which can cause harm to person, environment and property.

17
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:52,730
That is, it means safety.

18
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:58,530
From such conditions, freedom which can harm a person, environment and property.

19
00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:00,630
Second, what is hazard?

20
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:02,030
What is hazard?

21
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,130
You can answer it like this.

22
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:08,430
Hazard is anything or condition which has potential to cause harm.

23
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:12,830
That is, anything or condition which can cause harm,

24
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:14,230
is called hazard.

25
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:19,230
Such as sharp edge, unguarded working platform, slippery surface.

26
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:21,130
Third, what is risk?

27
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:22,530
That is, what is risk?

28
00:01:23,030 --> 00:01:24,630
You can answer it like this.

29
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:28,430
Risk is the probability of being harmed by any hazard.

30
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:33,130
That is, risk is the probability of being harmed by any hazard.

31
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:34,930
Next, what is injury?

32
00:01:35,130 --> 00:01:36,230
That is, what is injury?

33
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:38,430
You can answer it like this.

34
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:43,930
Injury is the harmful condition sustained by the body as a result of accident.

35
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:50,730
That is, injury is a harmful condition which has affected the body.

36
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:52,830
Next, what is accident?

37
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:54,430
That is, what is accident?

38
00:01:54,930 --> 00:01:56,530
You can answer it like this.

39
00:01:56,930 --> 00:02:01,630
Accident is an unwanted and unplanned event which can cause damage to property,

40
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,830
environment and even death to a person.

41
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:07,630
That is, accident is an unplanned or unwanted event

42
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:10,630
which can cause damage to property and environment

43
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,830
and also a person's death.

44
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,930
Next, what is near miss?

45
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:16,330
That is, what is near miss?

46
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:18,430
You can answer it like this.

47
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:22,830
Near miss is an unwanted and unplanned event which do not cause any harm.

48
00:02:23,330 --> 00:02:25,130
But it had potential to cause harm.

49
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:29,930
That is, near miss is an unwanted or unplanned event which do not cause any harm.

50
00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:32,430
But it had potential to cause harm.

51
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:35,730
We also call near miss to save lives.

52
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:39,730
Example, falling of a hammer without hitting anyone.

53
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:42,530
What are the common hazards at construction site?

54
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:45,730
That is, what are the common hazards on construction site?

55
00:02:45,930 --> 00:02:47,730
You can answer it like this.

56
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:51,930
Common hazards are moving object, for example, moving vehicle,

57
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:57,930
slip, trip and fall, noise, work at height hazards, manual handling,

58
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:03,530
collapse of soil, collapse of structure, asbestos, electricity, etc.

59
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:05,730
Next, what is work at height?

60
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:07,330
That is, what is work at height?

61
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:09,530
You can answer it like this.

62
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:13,130
Work at height means any work above 1.8 meter.

63
00:03:13,330 --> 00:03:17,530
That is, work at height is activity above 1.8 meter.

64
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:20,130
Next, question is, what is scaffolding?

65
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:21,730
That is, what is scaffolding?

66
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:23,930
You can answer it like this.

67
00:03:24,130 --> 00:03:29,330
Scaffolding is a temporary platform used to support man and material during work at height.

68
00:03:29,530 --> 00:03:31,730
That is, scaffolding is a temporary platform.

69
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:36,530
We use it to hold or support man and material at height.

70
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:38,930
Next, what are the types of scaffolding?

71
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:41,130
That is, how many types of scaffolding are there?

72
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:43,930
There are many types of scaffolding.

73
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,930
First is mobile scaffolding.

74
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:48,930
We can move this scaffolding from one place to another.

75
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:50,730
Next is static scaffolding.

76
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:52,730
We cannot move such scaffolding.

77
00:03:52,930 --> 00:03:54,730
There are examples of static scaffolding.

78
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:56,130
Cup lock scaffolding.

79
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:58,530
Next, cantilever scaffolding.

80
00:03:58,730 --> 00:04:00,730
Next, hanging scaffolding.

81
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:03,130
Next, bird cage scaffolding.

82
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:06,730
If you see according to OSHA, there are 10 types of scaffolding.

83
00:04:06,930 --> 00:04:08,930
OSHA's video link is pinned in the comment box.

84
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:10,130
You can check it now.

85
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:11,930
What are the hazards of scaffolding?

86
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,130
That is, what are the dangers of scaffolding?

87
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:17,130
First, use of damaged scaffolding components.

88
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:20,130
That is, use damaged components for scaffolding.

89
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:23,330
Second, scaffolding erection on uneven or loose ground.

90
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:26,530
That is, scaffolding on uneven or loose ground.

91
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:28,730
Third, improper tie and bracing.

92
00:04:28,930 --> 00:04:30,930
That is, not tying the scaffold properly.

93
00:04:31,130 --> 00:04:33,130
And bracing improper.

94
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:35,330
Fourth, fall of person and material.

95
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:37,530
That is, the danger of falling of person and material.

96
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:39,730
Fifth, improper guard rail.

97
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:41,930
That is, guard rail should not be right.

98
00:04:42,130 --> 00:04:43,930
Sixth, improper access.

99
00:04:44,130 --> 00:04:46,130
That is, the way to go is not right.

100
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:50,130
Next question is, what are the safety measures for scaffolding erection?

101
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:52,330
You can answer this.

102
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:54,530
First, all scaffolders must be competent.

103
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:56,730
All scaffolders must be competent.

104
00:04:56,930 --> 00:05:00,930
Second, scaffolding material must be sound and as per standard.

105
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:04,130
That is, scaffolding material should be in good condition.

106
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:06,330
Third, ground must be even and strong.

107
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:08,530
Ground should be even and strong.

108
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:11,730
Fourth, scaffolding must be tied if required.

109
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,930
And bracing must be provided.

110
00:05:13,930 --> 00:05:19,930
Fifth, top rail, mid rail, toe board, drop bar, base plate, scaffolding must be provided.

111
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:23,130
Next question is, what are the components of scaffolding?

112
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:25,330
That is, what are the components of scaffolding?

113
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:28,530
So, there are many components of scaffolding.

114
00:05:28,730 --> 00:05:33,730
First, soleboard, second, base plate, third, ledger.

115
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:35,930
Fourth, dressings.

116
00:05:36,130 --> 00:05:37,130
Fifth, standard.

117
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:39,330
Sixth, couplers.

118
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:41,530
Seventh, scaffolding.

119
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:43,530
Sixth, couplers.

120
00:05:43,730 --> 00:05:45,730
Seventh, scaffolding plank.

121
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:51,930
Eight, toe board, ninth, mid rail, tenth, top rail, eleventh, drop bar, etc.

122
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:55,130
Next question is, what is the height of top rail?

123
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:57,330
That is, what is the height of top rail?

124
00:05:57,530 --> 00:06:00,530
So, the answer is between 38 inches and 45 inches.

125
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:03,730
Next question is, what is the safe angle of ladder?

126
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:05,930
That is, what is the safe angle of ladder?

127
00:06:06,130 --> 00:06:09,130
So, the answer is 75 degrees.

128
00:06:09,330 --> 00:06:10,330
Next question is,

129
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:13,330
how much a ladder should be extended from the working platform?

130
00:06:13,530 --> 00:06:16,530
That is, how high should it be from the ladder platform?

131
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:20,730
So, the answer is, minimum of 1M, 3 feet.

132
00:06:20,930 --> 00:06:23,930
Next question is, can you ask about safety net?

133
00:06:24,130 --> 00:06:27,130
For safety net, the video link is in the comment box.

134
00:06:27,330 --> 00:06:28,330
You can check.

135
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:31,530
Next, what is the hierarchy of risk control?

136
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:34,730
That is, what is the hierarchy for risk control?

137
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:36,930
You can answer this.

138
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:40,130
The hierarchy of control is a system

139
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:42,330
for controlling risks in the workplace.

140
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:45,530
That is, the hierarchy of risk control is a system

141
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:47,730
which controls the risk.

142
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:49,930
There are five terms in this.

143
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:53,130
Elimination, Substitution,

144
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:56,330
Engineering Control, Administrative Control,

145
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:58,530
and Personal Protective Equipment.

146
00:06:58,730 --> 00:07:00,730
What is elimination?

147
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:04,930
Elimination means completely removing the hazard.

148
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,130
This is an example.

149
00:07:07,330 --> 00:07:09,330
Suppose there is a fan on a height.

150
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:11,330
It has a wing damage.

151
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:13,530
To replace the damage wing,

152
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:16,730
a temporary platform has been made.

153
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:19,930
If a worker changes the wing after standing on the platform,

154
00:07:20,130 --> 00:07:23,130
then there is the risk of fall of person and material.

155
00:07:23,330 --> 00:07:26,330
And if we bring the fan to the ground and then change the wing,

156
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:29,530
then there will be no risk of fall of person and material.

157
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:31,730
So, this method is elimination.

158
00:07:31,930 --> 00:07:33,930
Elimination is the most effective method

159
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:37,130
because the hazard is completely removed here.

160
00:07:37,130 --> 00:07:40,130
Next, Substitution.

161
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:43,330
Substitution means minimizing the hazard.

162
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:45,530
Come, let's take an example.

163
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:48,730
Suppose you have to do a job in a confined space.

164
00:07:48,930 --> 00:07:51,930
In a confined space, there can be flammable gas.

165
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:55,130
And because of this, there is a risk of fire.

166
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:58,330
And if you do a job in a confined space,

167
00:07:58,530 --> 00:08:00,530
then there is a risk of flammable gas.

168
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,730
And if you do a job in a confined space,

169
00:08:02,930 --> 00:08:04,930
then there is a risk of flammable gas.

170
00:08:04,930 --> 00:08:06,930
And because of this, there is a risk of fire.

171
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:10,130
If there is a problem of lighting in a confined space,

172
00:08:10,330 --> 00:08:12,330
then we use a bulb or a lamp for light.

173
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:17,530
If we use the electricity of 240 volts for sufficient light,

174
00:08:17,730 --> 00:08:20,730
then if there is a short circuit due to some fault,

175
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:23,930
then there can be a fire accident due to spark.

176
00:08:24,130 --> 00:08:29,130
So, to reduce this risk, we use 24 volt electricity

177
00:08:29,330 --> 00:08:33,330
so that the risk of spark and the chances of fire are less.

178
00:08:33,330 --> 00:08:35,330
So, we call this method substitution.

179
00:08:35,530 --> 00:08:37,530
Next, engineering control.

180
00:08:37,730 --> 00:08:41,730
In this method, we isolate the hazard from the engineering method.

181
00:08:41,930 --> 00:08:44,930
For example, if there is a rotating part of a machine,

182
00:08:45,130 --> 00:08:47,130
then place a cover guard on it.

183
00:08:47,330 --> 00:08:49,330
So that there is no contact in the rotating part.

184
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:52,530
Or any kind of auto-stop device.

185
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:55,730
This type of control is called engineering control.

186
00:08:55,930 --> 00:08:58,930
Next, personal protective equipment.

187
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:01,130
After applying the first four methods,

188
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:06,130
we use personal protective equipment for personal protection.

189
00:09:06,330 --> 00:09:09,330
This last method is the least effective.

190
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:14,530
Because using personal protective equipment does not end the hazard,

191
00:09:14,730 --> 00:09:17,730
it becomes a barrier between the hazard and the person.

192
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:20,930
Next, what is hazard identification and risk assessment?

193
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:25,130
We call it hazard identification and risk assessment.

194
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:28,330
Hira is a formalized process through which

195
00:09:28,330 --> 00:09:33,330
the hazard is identified and risk assessment is done in any job.

196
00:09:33,530 --> 00:09:36,530
How does Hira do it and how is the format for it?

197
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:39,730
There are some terms that are important to know before that.

198
00:09:39,930 --> 00:09:41,930
First, hazard.

199
00:09:42,130 --> 00:09:47,130
Hazard means any object or condition that can harm a person or environment.

200
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:52,330
For example, working on unguarded platform and hot weather condition.

201
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,530
Second, risk.

202
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:56,530
Second, risk.

203
00:09:56,730 --> 00:10:00,730
The probability of harm from any hazard is called risk.

204
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:03,930
Risk is also a likelihood multiplied by severity.

205
00:10:04,130 --> 00:10:06,130
Third, what is likelihood?

206
00:10:06,330 --> 00:10:09,330
The likelihood is also called probability.

207
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:13,530
The likelihood means chances of a hazard occurring.

208
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:16,730
We call severity a consequence.

209
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:19,930
The severity means the impact of a hazard.

210
00:10:19,930 --> 00:10:23,930
We will understand the likelihood and severity in the risk matrix.

211
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:26,130
Risk matrix.

212
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:28,330
What is risk matrix?

213
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:34,530
Risk matrix is a tool that can calculate the risk level during risk assessment.

214
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:39,730
The table you are looking at right now is a risk matrix of 5 to 5.

215
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:42,930
The lowest risk level is given in this.

216
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:45,130
1 to 6 low risk.

217
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:47,330
Low risk is acceptable.

218
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:49,330
Medium risk.

219
00:10:49,530 --> 00:10:52,530
In medium risk condition, we can work with proper supervision and precautions.

220
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:54,730
15 to 25 high risk.

221
00:10:54,930 --> 00:10:56,930
High risk is not acceptable.

222
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:59,130
We cannot work in this condition.

223
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:03,330
Let us now understand how to calculate the risk level from risk matrix.

224
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:05,530
There are two scaffolding here.

225
00:11:05,730 --> 00:11:07,730
There are guardrails in the first scaffolding.

226
00:11:07,930 --> 00:11:09,930
There are no guardrails in the second scaffolding.

227
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:12,130
The height of the scaffolding is 15 feet.

228
00:11:12,330 --> 00:11:15,330
The height of the scaffolding is 5 feet.

229
00:11:15,330 --> 00:11:19,330
When we work on scaffolding, there is a risk of fall of a person.

230
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:22,530
Now we will calculate the risk level of both the scaffolding.

231
00:11:22,730 --> 00:11:25,730
Risk is equal to probability into consequences.

232
00:11:25,930 --> 00:11:30,930
If there are guardrails in the first scaffolding, the chances of fall are unlikely.

233
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:33,130
So there are probability 2 here.

234
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:35,330
The height of the first scaffolding is 15 feet.

235
00:11:35,530 --> 00:11:39,530
The fatality can be caused by falling from here.

236
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:41,730
So the severity is very high.

237
00:11:41,730 --> 00:11:45,730
So in the first case, the risk level is 2 to 5, i.e. 10.

238
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:47,930
There are 10 medium risk in the risk matrix.

239
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:50,130
Now the second scaffolding.

240
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:52,330
There are no guardrails in the second scaffolding.

241
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:55,530
So the risk of fall here is very likely, i.e. much more.

242
00:11:55,730 --> 00:11:57,730
i.e. probability is 5.

243
00:11:57,930 --> 00:11:59,930
The height of the scaffolding is 5 feet.

244
00:12:00,130 --> 00:12:03,130
The fracture and serious injury can be caused by falling from this height.

245
00:12:03,330 --> 00:12:06,330
So the severity here is moderate, i.e. 3.

246
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:09,530
So the risk level is 3 to 5, i.e. 15.

247
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:12,530
There are 15 high risk levels in the risk matrix.

248
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:14,730
So you can calculate the risk like this.

249
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:19,930
The risk level can be high or low according to the location and job condition.

250
00:12:20,130 --> 00:12:23,130
Now let's understand the format. How to prepare the diamond?

251
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:25,330
So let's prepare the format first.

252
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:29,530
First, title, hazard identification and risk assessment.

253
00:12:29,730 --> 00:12:33,730
Second, job, work above 5 feet on scaffold.

254
00:12:33,930 --> 00:12:34,930
This is just an example.

255
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:39,130
If you want to download the JSA and the diamond, then search on Google.

256
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:43,130
www.safetymgmtstudy.com

257
00:12:43,330 --> 00:12:46,330
Next, serial number. Next, hazard.

258
